<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan yarn rates end stable, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Pakistan yarn rates end stable, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan cotton yarn rates were stable on Monday amid rising export demand and were likely to rise soon on fresh export orders, dealers said.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Monday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    455	    455</p>
<p>    Popular (Shabaz)	   435	    435</p>
<p>    Din Tex.		     460	    460</p>
<p>($1=40.62 rupees) Ovais Subhani (9221) 5685192; Fax 5673428</p>
